"><label class="field"><span>CSV file</span><input type="file" id="salesFile" name="salesFile" accept=".csv,.txt,text/csv" required></label><label class="field"><span>Force location</span><select id="uploadLocation" name="locationId"><option value="">Use CSV / all locations</option></select></label><button class="btn dark" type="submit">Import sales</button></div><div class="note"><strong>Minimum:</strong> a date column plus sales metrics. Recognized aliases include business_date, net_sales/revenue/sales, tickets/checks/orders, covers/guests, item_name/product, quantity/units_sold, category, hour and service_period/daypart. Weekly rows can use period_end or granularity=weekly. Monthly rows can use YYYY-MM or granularity=monthly. Aggregate files remain aggregate and are never silently divided into daily figures.</div><div id="uploadStatus" class="status"></div></form></div></section><?php endif;?><section class="tabpane panel" data-pane="periods"><div class="head"><h2>Aggregate period tracking</h2><span class="note">Weekly and monthly source totals</span></div><div class="body" id="periodTable"></div></section><section class="tabpane panel" data-pane="history"><div class="head"><h2>Import history</h2><span class="note">Checksum dedupe + rejected row counts</span></div><div class="body" id="importTable"></div></section><section class="tabpane panel" data-pane="connections"><div class="head"><h2>POS connections</h2><span class="note">CSV is active now; API adapters use the same ledger</span></div><div class="body"><div class="providers" id="providers"></div><p class="note">Toast credentials stay in server environment configuration, never in imported files or the Gelato database. Once Toast access is supplied, the connector can authenticate using Toast's machine-client flow and restaurant GUID. Square, Clover and other providers can plug into the same normalized sales layer later.</p></div></section></main><?php if($canAgent):?><div class="agent-bar"><input id="agentInput" placeholder="Hey Gelato… forecast Saturday dinner, show top items, what was labor percent last week?"><button id="agentSend">↑</button></div><?php endif;?><div class="toast hidden" id="toast"></div><script>window.SALES_CONFIG={csrf:<?=json_encode(app_csrf_token(),JSON_HEX_TAG|JSON_HEX_AMP|JSON_HEX_APOS|JSON_HEX_QUOT)?>,canImport:<?=$canImport?'true':'false'?>,canAgent:<?=$canAgent?'true':'false'?>,canIntegrations:<?=$canIntegrations?'true':'false'?>};</script><script src="js/sales-intelligence.js?v=20260914-1"></script><script src="js/universal-admin-page-shell.js?v=20260915-1"></script>
